{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:04:40.856018Z","id":"4ba1bef88ebee53d292310430277264c9ef9869541a73a5d4f6f351041abf6c7","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs measures artifact at 64069 gzip bytes against a budget of 64006 on bbc15627 itself (built from git archive in a scratch copy), so the bundle gate fails before and after the People page, whose change leaves the artifact entry at exactly 64069. Either trim the artifact entry or set its budget deliberately.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"03497708e9bcb00afb12a07f9067b13d6cf757e45d9906b71e1d98901e1f7eee"},"summary":"The artifact entry is over its budget at bbc15627","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:37:47.228703Z","id":"ef25f5928ead5b4920d5d7305ca71fe4423abc5223ed7e31bfce165c5ae7558c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4ba1bef88ebee53d292310430277264c9ef9869541a73a5d4f6f351041abf6c7","summary":"Measured per commit (npm run build, node scripts/bundle-size.mjs): 64006 at ffd6520b, the last deliberate raise; 4871da0f +14 (x-clax-via: page on the assets, db and comments capabilities), bba24eb6 +43 (threads.ts sendToAgent's page marker and approval routing), 9028b32f +6 (the agents event refetch in the artifact view); 64069 from 9028b32f on, unchanged by f2d449fc. The growth is spec-required behaviour in the artifact view, 0.1% of the entry.","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:02:20.888691Z","id":"771208c5bda950dac2d8d1c4822cdc9ad7ed45112cc1341fef029df463fb331c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:900e6485","summary":"The budget is 64069 in web/perf/bundle-budget.json. Evidence: npm run build && node scripts/bundle-size.mjs exits 0 with 'artifact 64069' after 55443491.","supersedes":"4ba1bef88ebee53d292310430277264c9ef9869541a73a5d4f6f351041abf6c7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.815194Z","id":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","body":{"detail":"The panel embeds the shell's Sidebar, ThreadCard and SendButton; the owner chip, the withheld label and the Send menu's grouping brought it to 65396 gzip bytes (from 65043), with the menu and the approval card moved into lazy chunks. The extension's own Send menu names (plan Task 23) have almost no room.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"935c259722638f24eea9dd631ad2e5f8cc1da6109229199e3b748da29265c76f"},"summary":"The extension panel is 140 bytes under its 65536 ceiling","tags":["task:23","bundle","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.164076Z","id":"ff328e16b94a81723262286df965f61e4eb3a5dd1c0f97ca35e60b70ba87c4ba","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","summary":"Confirmed with both builds' scripts/bundle-size.mjs: extension panel 65043 gzip bytes at a2378555, 65396 at f7a89d53 (ceiling 65536); questions 15125 -> 15564, people 12525 -> 12587; artifact unchanged at 64069, which equals its budget. The panel embeds the shell's SendButton and its lazy SendMenu, so names and person groups reach the extension's Send menu once its agents carry name and person; the panel's link from an approval item to the shell's inbox (spec 2026-10-08 section 17) is the next code to land there. Recommendation: decide the panel ceiling before that work (for example 66560, with a note of what grew) rather than squeezing; the 140 bytes left will not hold a link component and its styles.","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.260982Z","id":"2c03296e1e23090fbcdd86127cab3e21dd0ce1138e46921239907b0abf128436","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ff328e16b94a81723262286df965f61e4eb3a5dd1c0f97ca35e60b70ba87c4ba","summary":"After the round-1 fixes (bb547990) the extension panel measures 65526 of 65536 gzip bytes (10 left); the artifact entry measures 64062 of 64069, its Send default moved into the sidebar chunk.","tags":["bundle","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:40:37.891674Z","id":"ca2f1e9d1f8982634c233f3f36d8c5f2b825007457a5794e18be6e2eee744a14","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a3ae32de","summary":"The owner raised extPanel to 66560 (874f36ab). With the panel's Send rule, the worker's approves-first lookup and the approval rows' link (a3ae32de), node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs measures: panel 66388 of 66560, artifact 64062 of 64069 and gallery 27929 of 27960 (both unchanged from 086b92c8), questions 15608 of 16384.","supersedes":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.546920Z","id":"8653ded3974d2ab20916ce90da29649c32a3b18fa4e767b1c459629d978dddc4","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §23: the people module is lazy (16 KiB), gallery and artifact grow by at most 512 bytes, extPanel stays within 65,536. Measured at 09672011 (node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs): panel 66,555 against 66,560 (raised in 874f36ab), artifact 64,062 against 64,069 (63,988 at the branch's base: 74 bytes over main, within the 512), people 13,636 against 16,384, gallery 27,929 against 27,960. Either the panel sheds about 1 KiB (for one, its Send menu and approval items loaded when first opened) or the spec's 65,536 is amended; the artifact entry needs room before its next change, up to main's size plus 512 once the branch is rebased and main's sizes measured again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"bba27ecb5f1319da2af32bd259747e5f7245ba1bf7c1bc3fdbd2e87c31338ae2"},"summary":"extPanel's budget, 66,560 gzip bytes, is over spec §23's 65,536; the artifact entry has 7 bytes left","tags":["bundle","spec:23","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:19:10.697502Z","id":"8fd02f31348811e5b1d7c3d9a8b28466efd7b2bbc8aeb062ae20f0240be0384e","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs on npm run build of git archives (gzip bytes). artifact: 64006 at 8a2ff314^ and at 408f6d5d (W1's scroll code moved into the caps part by 31fdb579), 64180 at a8c8dc35^ (+174, app mode's eager seams: the ?app=1 check and lazy host import, ArtifactMount.controller(), the controller's app hooks, Send label; bba79ce3, 130e2614), 64370 at a8c8dc35 (+190, db.artifact(id)'s eager seam; the cross-read code is a lazy chunk), 64370 at f3e76c62. Budget 64390 since 0bfa971b (overage 364 rounded up to 384; 20 bytes of headroom). eager bridge: 5462 at 8a2ff314^, 5492 at 408f6d5d (+30, W1 long-press), 5493 at a8c8dc35 (+1), 5508 at f3e76c62 (+15, the pick start's element description, d8e1224c). Budget 5565 since 0bfa971b (57 bytes of headroom). Inside their budgets and unchanged: caps part 8144 -> 8492 (W1 scroll report and restore, 31fdb579) -> 8691 (W3, a8c8dc35), 82 bytes under 8773; comment part 10825 -> 11722 (W1 long-press) -> 11785 (W2 labels, d8e1224c), 36 bytes under 11821.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"59d05d05ba1f7453f5cbfd1e616f75fb3d9f36331c2bfba4b4df32ce0ea3f2b3"},"summary":"Why artifact, bridge and the caps and comment parts grew from W1 to W3 of the Flutter app plan, measured per commit","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/usable.perf.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:19:10.697702Z","id":"fd67d2733fa972fb59c7a3bb2e4f3d94cc4eb64794a6f519dc142f97f429df5f","body":{"detail":"Every measured link in web/perf/usable.perf.ts is the browser's view. In the app's view (web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts) the host message ready that stops the app's say-usable timer is posted only after the host-*.js chunk loads, so a regression in that chunk's size or load order moves say-usable without failing any gate. The browser view's numbers were unchanged by app mode: interleaved CLAX_PERF_QUICK=1 runs with web/dist from 8a2ff314^ and from f3e76c62 gave subdomain comment ready 84-102 ms and 85-105 ms at load average 9-10.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"71bda7919e5acd788c965c91cd7b3d6d28c2d33515ef8f081f0fc2b1a36b0517"},"suggested_fix":"Add an app-mode case to usable.perf.ts: open /a/<id>?app=1 with a stubbed window.ClaxHost (as web/e2e/app-host.ts does) and time link -> ready, with a recorded budget.","summary":"The time-to-usable gate opens /a/<id> without ?app=1: the Clax app's view, whose ready waits for the lazy host chunk, has no browser-side time budget","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/usable.perf.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:58:08.390341Z","id":"09adfd4a0840cb87b9f900ab78e8672f649f02bd507a5ff63523aa8f28a02697","body":{"detail":"The app's defended say-usable number stops on the shell's first `ready` (AppScreen.onReady, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:87-89), and on the phone app mode is the only view. That `ready` is posted from web/shell/src/app/host.ts:172 only once the lazy host chunk (dist/_clax/shell/host-*.js, 3677 gzip bytes at 4928617e) has loaded, so its load and anything added before `ctl.app.welcome` move say-usable with no gate failing. Neither gate covers it: usable.perf.ts opens /a/<id> without ?app=1, and web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs:98 measures the artifact entry and the eager bridge but not the host chunk.","kind":"comment","references":"fd67d2733fa972fb59c7a3bb2e4f3d94cc4eb64794a6f519dc142f97f429df5f","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"71bda7919e5acd788c965c91cd7b3d6d28c2d33515ef8f081f0fc2b1a36b0517"},"suggested_fix":"Add an app-mode case to usable.perf.ts: a context with a stubbed window.ClaxHost (as web/e2e/app-host.ts installs it) and the init call, open /a/<id>?app=1, time link -> first `ready` per frame mode, record its baseline and budget in web/perf/budget.json with CLAX_PERF_RECORD, and enforce it like commentReady.","summary":"Review of 42804f0f..4928617e: this gap blocks the Flutter app's web track (plan Task W4), not a follow-up","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/usable.perf.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:50.264319Z","id":"dcfadfe2703e0922d0b7650730e0735f4fa691f97322654e00f1e6a846ec99ae","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1a8f0d9","summary":"f1a8f0d9 adds appReady (link -> the shell's first ready to a stubbed ClaxHost, init as soon as window.claxHost is defined) to every sample in both frame modes, with a darwin-arm64 baseline recorded by CLAX_PERF_RECORD=baseline at load average 5.6-6.0: subdomain 45 ms (budget 75), sandbox 42 ms (budget 72). Later CLAX_PERF_QUICK=1 runs measured app ready 41-48 ms against limits 75-92 in both modes, at load 4-21.","supersedes":"fd67d2733fa972fb59c7a3bb2e4f3d94cc4eb64794a6f519dc142f97f429df5f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:27.683825Z","id":"4a9f0d8becfb6bb20cfbf413cd5fca769f6af2d0f37abaae6731c0fd4431acc8","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs (HEAD's copy) on npm run build of git archives of web/ and Cargo.toml, gzip bytes. Baseline 249c0bf5 (the last budget raise). artifact: 64519 at 249c0bf5 -> 64577 at 93fb5a63 (+58, inspect view and composeArtifact seams) -> 64728 at 29ccd4a1 (+151, an attested press counted as the finger's arrival) -> 64751 at 049d66cb (+23) -> 64756 at f64a72a8 (+5, the inspect frame name); unchanged through c42d1027, 0431fe45, c21cb615. eager bridge: 5508 at 249c0bf5 -> 5915 at 93fb5a63 (+407, the eager error ring) -> 5934 at a92f236b (+19, hold-then-drag chip) -> 5754 at 049d66cb (-180, ring kept raw and only in the inspect frame). This eager growth (+246) loads on every page. app host: 3896 at b8f55b02 -> 3927 at 249c0bf5 (+31, the animation-frame and visibility work of 3c6753c7, 11eaece3, 7e17f1aa) -> 4952 at 93fb5a63 (+1025, inspect, inspection, composeArtifact) -> 4999 at 29ccd4a1 (+47) -> 5062 at 52afbbe1 (+63, held-press expiry and cancel) -> 6081 at c42d1027 (+1019, the questions sheet) -> 6393 at 0431fe45 (+312, openQuestions by ID, closeQuestions, showing) -> 6400 at c21cb615 (+7). comment part: 11823 at 249c0bf5 -> 12310 at e0fafd0b (+487, hold then drag) -> 13036 at a92f236b (+726, the Comment chip offer). clip part: 15004 at 249c0bf5 -> 16476 at 93fb5a63 (+1472, settle, outline and renderViewport) -> 17336 at 049d66cb (+860, faithfulClone placeholders and broken images). Budgets since 608c2e33: measured plus at least 32 bytes, rounded up to a multiple of 64 (artifact 64832, host 6464, bridge 5824, comment 13120, clip 17408). Inside unchanged budgets: questions 14194 -> 14347 (c42d1027 +142, 0431fe45 +11) under the 16384 ceiling; extension overlay 18988 -> 20268 (hold-then-drag in the shared bridge code, e0fafd0b, a92f236b) under 32768.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":9},"content_hash":"b7be26657eb97721bfb164821092102a2e755e891145c8d0c133860b486f774c"},"summary":"Why artifact, app host, eager bridge and the comment and clip parts grew in round 2 of the Flutter app plan, measured per commit","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
